#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola with Vertex at the Origin Given Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "738f6646-2b0e-54a7-a66f-3f88a8fb5332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266668} {:answer/id #uuid "df0c7e8f-120b-51df-9fcb-2fe4352cea5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266669} {:answer/id #uuid "b5186bb9-878d-5662-845c-aec58d799d7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266670} {:answer/id #uuid "38e7bf11-4c43-55d5-9f7a-637bdbf27ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-16x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266671} {:answer/id #uuid "13a8146a-a778-5a19-9a8d-732040bc9426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df0c7e8f-120b-51df-9fcb-2fe4352cea5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266669} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cdc193e-5221-50b3-b374-abfd779910bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03ff4c40-b67c-529b-8313-05d8daa83019" :question/math-academy-id "q-115631" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at  $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(8,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(8,-4),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=-4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 16 & =32p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186356973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69a0dbc2-368b-50cf-8181-53aaf11d8756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356975} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc6ebe0-056c-5db3-aa4d-00da2d08a862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356976} {:answer/id #uuid "a99a99b6-7751-5bd4-87be-086d24316fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=3(x+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356977} {:answer/id #uuid "36fa5fed-3280-56d5-b4a5-e6d52d91da01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356978} {:answer/id #uuid "88381818-e2b1-51c9-9e9e-465ad7fc25b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}=3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cc6ebe0-056c-5db3-aa4d-00da2d08a862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356976} :answer-field/id #uuid "07b63f6e-8114-5be1-acc3-057df4a03f76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77c89899-e75a-59ab-bd2e-ad4bcdbad022" :question/math-academy-id "q-115643" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/assets/1f6330a6e9bc0e48326982c7b7509f3e2257de994c5736c813ede93a07491e70.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,-3)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(0,-3),$ we substitute $h=0$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (0+3)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 9 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{4})x \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{3}{4}$ is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186356980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola Given the Vertex and Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42d05c86-a4fd-5d27-a816-2fb3d493a1c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-3)^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356982} {:answer/id #uuid "9efed647-67d0-564d-9911-ad62bb315100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=36(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356983} {:answer/id #uuid "384be47f-c0e6-5e19-8751-565d9f5e163e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356984} {:answer/id #uuid "4d98b6c9-d61a-5361-a763-b6e14255ae15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}=-9(y-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356985} {:answer/id #uuid "2e909bea-71d8-5738-acdb-2bbf15181ddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=\\frac{9}{8}(x+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "384be47f-c0e6-5e19-8751-565d9f5e163e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356984} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e5a7402-d90a-5909-85eb-d6a5f0698f31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6abb456a-0967-521f-9352-1d7bccf90856" :question/math-academy-id "q-115646" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(1,-3)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(1,-3),$ we substitute $h=1$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (0+3)^{2} & =4p(3-1) \\\\ 9 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{8})(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{9}{2}(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola with Vertex at the Origin Given Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "033224ba-3b4c-5bed-8ccc-9b34855442cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266731} {:answer/id #uuid "cc1e5fc7-988e-577b-a6d4-07423d4ed819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266732} {:answer/id #uuid "2749846f-ba01-5229-b433-624512db0aaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266733} {:answer/id #uuid "aec062f0-2dbd-5eb0-9341-c573aaeca55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266734} {:answer/id #uuid "cbdef78f-8bc9-5385-8bb2-1d6a7e36e5d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "033224ba-3b4c-5bed-8ccc-9b34855442cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266731} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef4c39e-ea29-5165-8291-137d4b572f62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "07838d7d-bdf0-550d-9b73-045741b48872" :question/math-academy-id "q-11757" :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-6,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-6,-4),$ we can substitute $x=-6$ and $y=-4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 16 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{2}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{8}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola Given the Vertex and Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ff4c6d0-5c24-5fcd-9fca-9dfd778178ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=-(x+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266759} {:answer/id #uuid "2d3da3fb-9648-5131-9c99-e17ca9473916" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=2(x+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266760} {:answer/id #uuid "97c33400-48bb-59ea-9a6c-72d6af92c00c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266761} {:answer/id #uuid "1ca4baf0-5ed6-5664-b35c-c3a4cfea5285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266762} {:answer/id #uuid "be118941-1ee9-5e27-823e-cc3faced7134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=-2(x+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ca4baf0-5ed6-5664-b35c-c3a4cfea5285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266762} :answer-field/id #uuid "c959057f-8262-51b9-9ad1-345ef50afa38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3bdf088-2670-5350-9585-84f5c57baf89" :question/math-academy-id "q-11800" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(-4,-1)$ and passes through the point $(5,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-4,-1),$ we substitute $h=-4$ and $k=-1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(5,2),$ so we can substitute $x=5$ and $y=2$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (2+1)^{2} & =4p(5+4) \\\\ 9 & =36p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{4})(x+4) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
